---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Terms and Conditions | 3D Tesla Roadster Game" 
  description="Review the terms and conditions of use for the 3D Tesla Roadster Game. Fair use guidelines, WebGL simulator licensing, intellectual property notice, and user agreement."
  canonical="https://roadster-play.vercel.app/terms"
  keywords="Terms and conditions Tesla Roadster game, terms of service, WebGL simulator license, fair play policy, hypercar game agreement, fan project terms"
>
  <!-- Schema.org Structured Data: WebPage & BreadcrumbList -->
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "name": "Terms and Conditions - 3D Tesla Roadster Game",
    "url": "https://roadster-play.vercel.app/terms",
    "description": "Terms of service, user agreement, and non-commercial fan disclaimer for the 3D Tesla Roadster Game WebGL simulator.",
    "breadcrumb": {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Home",
          "item": "https://roadster-play.vercel.app/"
        },
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "name": "Terms & Conditions",
          "item": "https://roadster-play.vercel.app/terms"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  </script>

  <div style="max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 5rem;">
    
    <!-- Breadcrumb Navigation -->
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <ol style="list-style: none; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; font-size: 13px; color: var(--mute); padding: 0; margin: 0; font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace;">
        <li><a href="/" class="nav-link" style="padding: 0;">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-hidden="true" style="color: var(--faint);">/</li>
        <li aria-current="page" style="color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600;">Terms &amp; Conditions</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- Page Header / Hero -->
    <header style="margin-bottom: 3.5rem;">
      <span class="mono-eyebrow" style="color: var(--link);">USER AGREEMENT &amp; GUIDELINES</span>
      <h1 class="display-xl" style="margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--ink);">
        Terms and Conditions
      </h1>
      <p class="body-md" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; color: var(--mute); font-family: 'Geist Mono', monospace;">
        EFFECTIVE DATE: OCTOBER 2026 &nbsp;•&nbsp; LAST REVISED: OCTOBER 29, 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Legal Highlight Banner: Disclaimer & Fan Project Notice -->
    <section class="vercel-card" style="padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 3.5rem; background: var(--canvas-elevated); border-left: 4px solid var(--link);">
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
        <span style="font-size: 1.25rem;">⚖️</span>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); font-size: 16px;">Core Disclaimers &amp; Fan Project Notice</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="body-sm" style="color: var(--body); line-height: 1.7;">
        The <strong>3D Tesla Roadster Game</strong> is an independent, non-commercial educational project created as an interactive tribute celebrating pioneering concepts in electric hypercar propulsion and aerospace engineering. 
        This website and simulator are <strong>NOT affiliated with, sponsored by, authorized by, or endorsed by Tesla, Inc. or Space Exploration Technologies Corp. (SpaceX)</strong>. 
        "Tesla", "Roadster", and "SpaceX" are registered trademarks of their respective owners.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Detailed Terms Articles -->
    <article style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3rem; color: var(--body); line-height: 1.7; font-size: 15px;">
      
      <!-- Article 1 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing, browsing, launching, or playing the 3D Tesla Roadster Game (the "Service," "Simulator," or "Website"), you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions ("Terms"). If you do not agree with any part of these Terms, you must discontinue using the Website and close the simulator immediately.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Article 2 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">2. License to Use the Simulator</h2>
        <p>
          Subject to your compliance with these Terms, we grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to access and execute the WebGL driving simulator strictly for personal, non-commercial entertainment and educational demonstration purposes through a standard web browser.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
          You agree not to:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin-top: 0.75rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem;">
          <li>Decompile, reverse engineer, or disassemble the client-side binary bundle or 3D asset geometry for commercial exploitation.</li>
          <li>Re-host, mirror, or frame the simulator within commercial paywalled portals or malicious ad-injection frames without explicit consent.</li>
          <li>Circumvent or tamper with in-game physics engines, telemetry timers, or local browser storage mechanisms in order to submit falsified leaderboards.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Article 3 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">3. Intellectual Property Rights</h2>
        <p>
          The custom software code, Three.js shaders, aerodynamic physics algorithms, procedural audio synthesis pipelines, Geist design implementation, and written content embodied within this Website are the intellectual property of the 3D Tesla Roadster Game open-source project contributors.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
          Vehicle names, model designs, and trademarks belonging to third parties (including Tesla Roadster, SpaceX, Rimac Nevera, Bugatti Tourbillon, and Porsche Taycan) are referenced strictly under nominative fair use doctrine to accurately identify and compare performance benchmarks.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Article 4 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">4. Acceptable Use &amp; Network Integrity</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to utilize the Website in accordance with all applicable international, national, and local laws. You shall not:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin-top: 0.75rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem;">
          <li>Engage in automated denial-of-service (DDoS) attacks, automated rapid-fire asset requests, or attempt to overwhelm our edge CDN infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Introduce viruses, worms, Trojan horses, logic bombs, or other malicious digital code.</li>
          <li>Harvest, scrape, or extract bulk data from the Website using automated bots without authorization.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Article 5 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">5. Simulation Physics &amp; Safety Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          The physics, acceleration rates (0–60 MPH in 0.58 seconds), SpaceX cold-gas thruster plumes, and 2G ground and wall suction mechanics modeled in this simulator are interactive digital calculations intended for entertainment and scientific curiosity. 
          They do not constitute real-world driving instructions or mechanical blueprints. 
          Real-world drivers must always obey local speed limits and traffic safety regulations.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Article 6 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">6. WebGL Hardware &amp; Performance Limitations</h2>
        <p>
          The simulator relies on WebGL 2.0 graphics rendering. Frame rates, latency, and visual fidelity are heavily dependent on your device's graphics processing unit (GPU), available system memory, display refresh rate, and browser efficiency. 
          We make no representation or guarantee that the simulation will achieve 60 FPS on older or unsupported hardware architectures.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Article 7 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">7. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          THE SIMULATOR AND ALL ASSOCIATED CONTENT ARE PROVIDED ON AN <strong>"AS IS"</strong> AND <strong>"AS AVAILABLE"</strong> BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EITHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, OR NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT THE SERVICE WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, ERROR-FREE, OR FREE OF GLITCHES.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Article 8 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED UNDER APPLICABLE LAW, IN NO EVENT SHALL THE DEVELOPERS, CONTRIBUTORS, OR AFFILIATES OF THIS PROJECT BE LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH YOUR USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SIMULATOR, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Article 9 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">9. Modifications to the Service and Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We reserve the right at any time to modify, suspend, or discontinue any feature, circuit, vehicle tuning, or gameplay mode of the simulator without prior notice. 
          We may also amend these Terms periodically. Continued access to the Website following updates constitutes binding agreement to the amended terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Article 10 -->
      <section style="border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); padding-top: 2rem;">
        <h2 class="heading-md" style="color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">10. Contact &amp; Legal Inquiries</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions, trademark feedback, or legal inquiries concerning these Terms and Conditions, please reach out to us via our dedicated communication portal:
        </p>
        <div style="margin-top: 1rem;">
          <a href="/contact" class="btn-pill-primary" style="height: 38px; padding: 0 18px; font-size: 13px;">
            Visit Contact Portal →
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

    </article>

  </div>
</Layout>
